<title>BRAZIL: Confab, Marubeni in Petrobras deal.</title>
<headline>Confab, Marubeni in Petrobras deal.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Confab and Japan's Marubeni Corp said they will sign Wednesday a $628 million agreement with Petrobras to supply steel pipes for the Brazil-Bolivia gas pipeline.</p>
<p>Confab, Brazil's largest capital goods producer, will supply $476 million in steel pipes for the Brazilian side, while Japanese trading firm Marubeni will supply the remaining $170 million in pipes for the Bolivian side, a Confab spokeswoman said.  The two companies will supply 540,000 tonnes of steel pipes which will extend over a distance of 3,150 kilometers, she added.</p>
<p>Confab's sales reached $350 million in 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
